# Default-deny: only files explicitly COPY'd in the Dockerfile end up in
# the image. Without this file the entire build context (including
# `.env`, `.git`, the local `.venv`, test fixtures, IDE state, caches,
# and build artifacts) gets baked into the published layer.
#
# Security review (2026-04-30) confirmed `/app/.env` had been embedded
# in built images, exposing OPENBRIDGE_REFRESH_TOKEN values. This file
# closes that hole.
*

# Source we DO want — every entry below must match the COPY lines in
# the Dockerfile or it will be invisible to the build.
!main.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!schemas/

# Re-deny anything that snuck into the allow-listed dirs above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
